tnes 1.12.0 (fork of tines 1.12.0)

	* Renamed the program to tnes so it can coexist with tines.
	  It still uses the same database, configuration, and file
	  formats as tines.

	* Autosave on Enter: committing an entry (new node or edit)
	  now runs the same "save" command as F2.

	* Session restore: the cursor position and expanded nodes are
	  remembered in a <database>_tnes_session sidecar file and
	  restored on the next launch. Updated on every save, quit,
	  timed autosave, and keypress (written only when changed).

	* Session files are now written atomically (write to a temp
	  file, then rename), so a crash cannot leave a truncated
	  session file behind.

	* Session parsing hardened: values must be plain numbers
	  ("expanded banana" is ignored instead of being read as 0),
	  and a cursor saved at the first node is now restored too.

	* New commands: session_save, session_restore.

	* New files: src/session.c, src/session.h, tests/session-smoke.sh,
	  doc/tnes.1 (installed as the tnes manpage).

	* Fixed argv/database path buffer sizes (strncat-bounded copies
	  for argv[0] and the database argument, larger stack buffers
	  for rescue/session paths).

	* The binary now reports version 1.12.0, matching configure.ac
	  (src/config.h previously said 1.11.1).
